# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.25.1
ignore:
  SNYK-ALPINE323-P11KIT-17486696:
    - '*':
        reason: The services do not use remote PKCS#11 tokens or the IBM Kyber/BTC C_DeriveKey mechanisms required to exploit this issue.
        expires: 2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-GOLANG-GOLANGORGXNETHTTP2-16535157:
    - '*':
        reason: The vulnerable code is embedded in kubectl, which communicates only with the trusted Kubernetes API server.
        expires: 2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-GOLANG-GOLANGORGXNETIDNA-17116876:
    - '*':
        reason: Kubectl obtains the API server endpoint from trusted cluster configuration and does not validate attacker-controlled hostnames.
        expires: 2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-CHQOSLOGBACK-17675439:
    - '*':
        reason: Logback configuration is immutable at runtime and the service does not use Janino conditional configuration.
        expires: 2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-17972608:
    - '*':
        reason: The service does not combine JsonView and JsonUnwrapped annotations during deserialization.
        expires: 2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-IONETTY-18170202:
    - '*':
        reason: The service uses Spring MVC with Tomcat and does not install a Netty SPDY pipeline.
        expires: 2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-IONETTY-18170204:
